  "notes": "{突|つ}く means to poke or thrust with a forward motion. It is also used for propping or leaning body parts on a surface.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {嘘|うそ}をつく: to tell a lie\n- {肘|ひじ}をつく: to put one's elbows (on a table)\n- {杖|つえ}をつく: to use a cane\n- {膝|ひざ}をつく: to kneel (put one's knees to the ground)\n- {溜|た}め{息|いき}をつく: to sigh\n\nNOTE: Many of these expressions are commonly written in kana (つく) rather than with the kanji {突|つ}く.\n\nHOMOPHONES:\n- {付|つ}く: to be attached, to stick\n- {着|つ}く: to arrive\n- {就|つ}く: to take up (a position)",
